/// `binary-naturals`: Binary natural numbers.
// A numeral annotated `(n : Nat)` is the prelude's binary natural it names,
// its lowest digit outermost: five is one, zero, one read from the outside
// in, so the numeral converts with the term it names.

/// Five, its binary constructor term.
def five : Path(Nat, (5 : Nat), Positive(Bit1(Bit0(One)))) = here(Positive(Bit1(Bit0(One))));
